    whenToApply: "A handler checks req.destroyed, req.aborted, res.writableEnded or a socket flag to decide whether to abandon work, skip a write or stop an upload. Those flags read true during perfectly healthy requests once the body has been consumed, so real work is thrown away and the client is told nothing; the resulting failures look like network flakiness.",
